> Original diagonal classification fixture

Retain mt19937_64 seed3, 300 candidate pairs sampled x then y uniformly
on[-3,3], and discard pairs with abs(x+y)<0.3. Labels are1 when x+y>0. These are
training observations, not an independent test set. The table retains the
original five probability queries. A number near zero or one is a model
probability, not evidence that probabilities are calibrated.

The implementation sorts each feature but scans all n observations twice for
every candidate threshold. With at most n thresholds per feature, each round
costs O(d*n*n+d*n*log(n)), rather than the earlier report’s O(n*d) claim.
Ordinary fitting stores O(n+T) working/model data, excluding the input;
prediction sums T stumps. Public single-stump prediction validates the supplied
query, so the checked probability wrapper currently incurs O(T*d) validation as
well.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/logitboost_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/logitboost.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/logitboost_study.hpp>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto data = dm::algorithms::logitboost_diagonal_data();
    const auto &x = data.features;
    const auto &y = data.labels;
    auto m = dm::algorithms::logitboost_train(x, y, 40);
    std::size_t correct = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i)
        correct += dm::algorithms::logitboost_predict(m, x[i]) == y[i];
    std::print("Actual retained training rows {}; fitted rounds {}; training accuracy {}.\n\n| query x | " "query y | actual model probability |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               x.size(), m.stumps.size(), double(correct) / x.size());
    for (auto q : std::vector<std::vector<double>>{{3, 3}, {1, .5}, {0, .1},
                                                   {-1, -.5}, {-3, -3}})
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", q[0], q[1],
                   dm::algorithms::logitboost_probability(m, q));
    std::vector<double> a, b;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < m.log_likelihood.size(); ++i) {
        a.push_back(i + 1);
        b.push_back(m.log_likelihood[i]);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(a, b, "training diagnostic", {37, 99, 235}, 2).title(
        "Original diagonal fixture: actual training history").x_label(
        "committed boosting round").y_label("clipped-probability binomial log likelihood").save_svg("build/logitboost_original.svg");
}
```
